# INDEXLA APP — ALWAYS DEPLOY ON TASK COMPLETION

When any IndexLa-App task is finished (UI, routes, tests, content, or ops for the separate app):

## Required completion flow

1. Work only in `C:/Users/hp/Desktop/IndexLa-App` (never push app code into the website repo).
2. Run local verification relevant to the change (`typecheck` / `lint` / `test` / `build` / Playwright as needed).
3. Commit and push to `https://github.com/IdeatorYas/IndexlaApp` on branch `main`.
4. Deploy to production preview with the existing zero-downtime process only:
   - Package/upload app to `/var/www/IndexLa-App`
   - Run `/usr/local/bin/deploy-indexla-app.sh`
5. Verify live:
   - `https://app.indexla.tech/app` returns 200 and shows the intended change
   - `https://indexla.tech` remains healthy and untouched
6. Do not declare the app task complete until `app.indexla.tech` is verified live.

## Hard boundaries

- PM2 process: `indexla-app` on port **3001** only
- Website PM2 `indexla` on port **3000** must not be restarted or modified for app work
- Never deploy unfinished/failing builds over a healthy preview
- On deploy failure: keep previous known-good (`deploy-indexla-app.sh --restore-good`)

## Report when finished

Always include:

- Git commit hash + push status
- Deploy status
- Live URL confirmation for `app.indexla.tech`
- Confirmation that `indexla.tech` is still healthy
